  "mathematical_claims": [
    "For every finite prime set P, the complete same-P-free-core packet is nonnegative and at most kappa(P)*H_N.",
    "Whenever kappa(P_N)*H_N is subpower, all-rate control of the distinct P_N-free-core packet is equivalent to the full weighted-prefix endpoint supplier.",
    "For primes up to floor(log(N+1)), kappa(P_N)*H_N is subpower.",
    "The completely multiplicative prime-two sign satisfies every doubling identity and every same-odd-core chain identity, but its distinct-odd-core packet is at least N/128 for N>=2048.",
    "Therefore fixed finite-prime identities and positive orbit bounds cannot prove the actual distinct-odd-core supplier."
  ],
